   "subject": "extended.pgls and trajectory.analysis",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Dear geomorph community,<br><br>I am working on a phylogenetic control requested by reviewers, and I would like to know whether extended.pgls() can be combined with trajectory.analysis().<br><br>My data and design<br>- Multivariate shape data (48 variables) for 195 individuals of 6 species, with many individuals per species.<br>- Species = species (factor); Stage = an ordered three-level factor (e.g., low, medium and high wear: S1, S2, S3). The goal is to build one trajectory per species, with the three stages as trajectory points, and to compare trajectories among species (length, direction, shape).<br>- Phylogeny: a pruned cladogram with branch lengths assigned (Grafen), with tips matching the levels of Species.<br><br>What I did<br><br>Ordinary model (works as expected):<br><br>fit_ordinary &lt;- procD.lm(Y ~ Species * Stage, data = my_data, iter = 999)<br>TA_ordinary &lt;- trajectory.analysis(fit_ordinary, groups = my_data$Species,<br>                                   traj.pts = my_data$Stage, pca = TRUE)<br><br>Here the trajectory points are exactly equal to the species-by-stage means of the individual scores in the PC space returned by plot(TA_ordinary).<br><br>Phylogenetic model:<br><br>fit_phylo &lt;- extended.pgls(Y ~ Species * Stage, data = my_data,<br>                           species = &quot;Species&quot;, phy = my_tree, iter = 999)<br>TA_phylo &lt;- trajectory.analysis(fit_phylo, groups = my_data$Species,<br>                                traj.pts = my_data$Stage, pca = TRUE)<br><br>trajectory.analysis() runs without errors, but the trajectory points do not match the data. For example, for one species (Species_A), comparing the mean of the individual scores in each stage with the trajectory point, both in the PC space of TA_phylo:<br><br>          mean of individuals       trajectory point<br>          PC1       PC2             PC1       PC2<br>S1       -0.257     0.060          -2.609     0.061<br>S2       -0.141     0.030          -1.802    -0.431<br>S3        0.249     0.134           2.423     0.585<br><br>My questions<br>1. Is trajectory.analysis() intended to work with objects of class <a href=\"http://lm.rrpp.ws\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://lm.rrpp.ws&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793953739931000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1DWbPlO9yCNChEuk9OTKrs\">lm.rrpp.ws</a> returned by extended.pgls()? If not, is there a recommended way to run a trajectory analysis conditioned on the phylogeny when each trajectory corresponds to a different species?<br>2. Is there any  limitation when the groups used for the trajectories (Species) are also the species used in the phylogenetic covariance structure?<br><br>Some cells are small (for example, n = 2 individuals in a few species-by-stage combinations), in case this is relevant.<br><br>I can provide a reproducible example or share the data  if that would help.<br><br>Thank you very much for your time.<br><br>Best regards,<br>Ale<br><br>geomorph_4.1.1<br>RRPP_2.2.0 "
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "eoSimhmaAAAJ",
   "from": "Adams, Dean [EEOB]",
   "author": "4d71c6e24fb21497",
   "date": "2026-11-04T17:52:48Z",
   "subject": "Re: [geomorph-r-package] extended.pgls and trajectory.analysis",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nAle,</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nYes, trajectory.analysis can work with extended.pgls/<a href=\"http://lm.rrpp.ws\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://lm.rrpp.ws&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793953739935000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0DqPhHWCbd3bld7Hb5CWkM\">lm.rrpp.ws</a>.  In our 2024 paper where we introduced extended PGLS, we did precisely that in the pupfish example: extended PGLS + TA.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nHowever, I can replicate the shift in group means in the plot that you described, so a bug seems to have been introduced somewhere. </div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nWe will investigate that.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nDean</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;font-size:10pt;color:black\">Dr. Dean C. Adams</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;font-size:10pt;color:black\">Distinguished Professor</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;font-size:10pt;color:black\">Director, Ecology and Evolutionary Biology Graduate Program</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;font-size:10pt;color:black\">Department of Ecology, Evolution, and Organismal Biology</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;font-size:10pt;color:black\">Iowa State University</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;font-size:10pt;color:blue\"><a href=\"http://www.public.iastate.edu/~dcadams/\" style=\"color:blue;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.public.iastate.edu/~dcadams/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793953739935000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3f7ldrcth29Tc7uT44aSGw\"><u>www.public.iastate.edu/~dcadams/</u></a></span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;font-size:10pt;color:black\">phone: <a href=\"tel:(515)%20294-3834\" value=\"+15152943834\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">515-294-3834</a></span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in;font-fami