    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>Dear geomorph community,<br>\r\n<br>\r\nI am working on a phylogenetic control requested by reviewers, and I would like to know whether extended.pgls() can be combined with trajectory.analysis().<br>\r\n<br>\r\nMy data and design<br>\r\n- Multivariate shape data (48 variables) for 195 individuals of 6 species, with many individuals per species.<br>\r\n- Species = species (factor); Stage = an ordered three-level factor (e.g., low, medium and high wear: S1, S2, S3). The goal is to build one trajectory per species, with the three stages as trajectory points, and to compare trajectories among species (length,\r\n direction, shape).<br>\r\n- Phylogeny: a pruned cladogram with branch lengths assigned (Grafen), with tips matching the levels of Species.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nWhat I did<br>\r\n<br>\r\nOrdinary model (works as expected):<br>\r\n<br>\r\nfit_ordinary &lt;- procD.lm(Y ~ Species * Stage, data = my_data, iter = 999)<br>\r\nTA_ordinary &lt;- trajectory.analysis(fit_ordinary, groups = my_data$Species,<br>\r\n                                   traj.pts = my_data$Stage, pca = TRUE)<br>\r\n<br>\r\nHere the trajectory points are exactly equal to the species-by-stage means of the individual scores in the PC space returned by plot(TA_ordinary).<br>\r\n<br>\r\nPhylogenetic model:<br>\r\n<br>\r\nfit_phylo &lt;- extended.pgls(Y ~ Species * Stage, data = my_data,<br>\r\n                           species = &quot;Species&quot;, phy = my_tree, iter = 999)<br>\r\nTA_phylo &lt;- trajectory.analysis(fit_phylo, groups = my_data$Species,<br>\r\n                                traj.pts = my_data$Stage, pca = TRUE)<br>\r\n<br>\r\ntrajectory.analysis() runs without errors, but the trajectory points do not match the data. For example, for one species (Species_A), comparing the mean of the individual scores in each stage with the trajectory point, both in the PC space of TA_phylo:<br>\r\n<br>\r\n          mean of individuals       trajectory point<br>\r\n          PC1       PC2             PC1       PC2<br>\r\nS1       -0.257     0.060          -2.609     0.061<br>\r\nS2       -0.141     0.030          -1.802    -0.431<br>\r\nS3        0.249     0.134           2.423     0.585<br>\r\n<br>\r\nMy questions<br>\r\n1. Is trajectory.analysis() intended to work with objects of class <a href=\"http://lm.rrpp.ws\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://lm.rrpp.ws&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793953739935000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0DqPhHWCbd3bld7Hb5CWkM\">lm.rrpp.ws</a> returned by extended.pgls()? If not, is there a recommended way to run a trajectory analysis conditioned on the phylogeny when each trajectory corresponds to a different species?<br>\r\n2. Is there any  limitation when the groups used for the trajectories (Species) are also the species used in the phylogenetic covariance structure?<br>\r\n<br>\r\nSome cells are small (for example, n = 2 individuals in a few species-by-stage combinations), in case this is relevant.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nI can provide a reproducible example or share the data  if that would help.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nThank you very much for your time.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nBest regards,<br>\r\nAle<br>\r\n<br>\r\ngeomorph_4.1.1<br>\r\nRRPP_2.2.0\r\n<p></p></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;geomorph R package&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to\r\n<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-r-pack...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/geomorph-r-package/cbb6b0d7-9cd3-43bf-a6d0-ab4d56348312n%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/geomorph-r-package/cbb6b0d7-9cd3-43bf-a6d0-ab4d56348312n%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793953739935000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1AfxqBKtGsRT1KRC27wa1H\">\r\nhttps://groups.google.com/d/msgid/geomorph-r-package/cbb6b0d7-9cd3-43bf-a6d0-ab4d56348312n%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n"
