  {
   "id": "SyQRfuVOAAAJ",
   "from": "Mike Collyer",
   "author": "aab55242ff4da6c6",
   "date": "2026-11-04T23:06:18Z",
   "subject": "Re: [geomorph-r-package] extended.pgls and trajectory.analysis",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"line-break:after-white-space\">Dear Ale, and everyone,<div><br></div><div>The issue was caused by a missing phylogenetic transformation of the model matrix used to obtain least-squares means in the RRPP::pairwise function, used within trajectory.analysis (not extended.pgls).  I am hopeful this would cause no major issues with the trajectory analysis, itself, but just the resulting graph.  Phylogenetic transformations were used to obtain random pseudo-data via RRPP and the model matrix for LS means was constructed properly, but not having the phylogenetic transformation in the last step meant the LS means were shifted away from the origin in the PC plot.  This would be a consistent (affine) shift in each RRPP permutation.</div><div><br></div><div>Please re-install RRPP from my Gtihub (mlcollyer/RRPP) and see if your results make sense.  Let me know if issues persist.  I will soon send an update to CRAN, but wish to test the function more first.</div><div><br></div><div>Sorry for the bug!</div><div><br></div><div>Mike<br><div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On Nov 4, 2026, at 12:52 PM, &#39;Adams, Dean [EEOB]&#39; via geomorph R package &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-line:none;text-decoration-style:solid;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt\">Ale,</div><div style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-line:none;text-decoration-style:solid;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt\"><br></div><div style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-line:none;text-decoration-style:solid;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt\">Yes, trajectory.analysis can work with extended.pgls/<a href=\"http://lm.rrpp.ws\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://lm.rrpp.ws&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793953739942000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2ByK2AGaWcZXt_ZX3Sd10B\">lm.rrpp.ws</a>.  In our 2024 paper where we introduced extended PGLS, we did precisely that in the pupfish example: extended PGLS + TA.</div><div style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-line:none;text-decoration-style:solid;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt\"><br></div><div style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-line:none;text-decoration-style:solid;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt\">However, I can replicate the shift in group means in the plot that you described, so a bug seems to have been introduced somewhere. </div><div style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-line:none;text-decoration-style:solid;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt\"><br></div><div style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-line:none;text-decoration-style:solid;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt\">We will investigate that.</div><div style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-line:none;text-decoration-style:solid;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt\"><br></div><div style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-line:none;text-decoration-style:solid;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt\">Dean</div><div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-line:none;text-decoration-style:solid\"><div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0in;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;font-size:10pt\">Dr. Dean C. Adams</span></div><div style=\"margin:0in;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;font-size:10pt\">Distinguished Professor</span></div><div style=\"margin:0in;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;font-size:10pt\">Director, Ecology and Evolutionary Biology Graduate Program</span></div><div style=\"margin:0in;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;font-size:10pt\">Department of Ecology, Evolution, and Organismal Biology</span></div><div style=\"margin:0in;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;font-size:10pt\">Iowa State University</span></div><div style=\"margin:0in;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;font-size:10pt;color:blue\"><a href=\"http://www.public.iastate.edu/~dcadams/\" style=\"color:blue;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.public.iastate.edu/~dcadams/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793953739942000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0hOiycIvf8q-UoASsiNHKD\"><u>www.public.iastate.edu/~dcadams/</u></a></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;font-size:10pt\">phone: <a href=\"tel:(515)%20294-3834\" value=\"+15152943834\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">515-294-3834</a></span></div><p style=\"margin:0in;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt\"> </p><