\"><tr style=\"background:revert!important;border:revert!important;color:revert!important;direction:revert!important;display:revert!important;font-size:revert!important;height:revert!important;letter-spacing:revert!important;line-height:revert!important;margin:revert!important;opacity:revert!important;outline:revert!important;overflow:revert!important;padding:revert!important;table-layout:revert!important;text-align:revert!important;text-indent:revert!important;text-orientation:revert!important;text-overflow:revert!important;text-transform:revert!important;vertical-align:revert!important;white-space:revert!important;width:revert!important;word-break:revert!important;word-spacing:revert!important;writing-mode:revert!important;zoom:revert!important\"><td valign=\"middle\" width=\"1px\" bgcolor=\"#A6A6A6\" cellpadding=\"7px 2px 7px 2px\" style=\"background-image:revert!important;background-position:revert!important;background-size:revert!important;background-repeat:revert!important;background-origin:revert!important;background-clip:revert!important;border:revert!important;color:revert!important;direction:revert!important;display:revert!important;font-size:revert!important;height:revert!important;letter-spacing:revert!important;line-height:revert!important;margin:revert!important;opacity:revert!important;outline:revert!important;overflow:revert!important;table-layout:revert!important;text-align:revert!important;text-indent:revert!important;text-orientation:revert!important;text-overflow:revert!important;text-transform:revert!important;vertical-align:revert!important;white-space:revert!important;word-break:revert!important;word-spacing:revert!important;writing-mode:revert!important;zoom:revert!important;padding:7px 2px!important;background-color:rgb(166,166,166)!important;width:0px!important\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" width=\"100%\" bgcolor=\"#EAEAEA\" cellpadding=\"7px 5px 7px 15px\" style=\"background-image:revert!important;background-position:revert!important;background-size:revert!important;background-repeat:revert!important;background-origin:revert!important;background-clip:revert!important;border:revert!important;direction:revert!important;display:revert!important;height:revert!important;letter-spacing:revert!important;line-height:revert!important;margin:revert!important;opacity:revert!important;outline:revert!important;overflow:revert!important;table-layout:revert!important;text-indent:revert!important;text-orientation:revert!important;text-overflow:revert!important;text-transform:revert!important;vertical-align:revert!important;white-space:revert!important;word-break:revert!important;word-spacing:revert!important;writing-mode:revert!important;zoom:revert!important;width:532px;background-color:rgb(234,234,234)!important;padding:7px 5px 7px 15px!important;font-family:wf_segoe-ui_normal,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP&quot;,Tahoma,Arial,sans-serif!important;font-size:12px!important;font-weight:normal!important;color:rgb(33,33,33)!important;text-align:left!important\"><div style=\"background:revert!important;border:revert!important;color:revert!important;direction:revert!important;display:revert!important;font-size:revert!important;min-height:revert!important;letter-spacing:revert!important;line-height:revert!important;margin:revert!important;opacity:revert!important;outline:revert!important;overflow:revert!important;padding:revert!important;table-layout:revert!important;text-align:revert!important;text-indent:revert!important;text-orientation:revert!important;text-overflow:revert!important;text-transform:revert!important;vertical-align:revert!important;white-space:revert!important;width:revert!important;word-break:revert!important;word-spacing:revert!important;writing-mode:revert!important;zoom:revert!important\">You don&#39;t often get email from<span> </span><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">alej...@gmail.com</a>.<span> </span><a href=\"https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification\" style=\"background:revert!important;color:revert!important;direction:revert!important;display:revert!important;font-size:revert!important;opacity:revert!important\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793953739942000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0_NonZayq0YIZiiZyfdQNo\">Learn why this is important</a></div></td><td valign=\"middle\" align=\"left\" width=\"75px\" bgcolor=\"#EAEAEA\" cellpadding=\"7px 5px 7px 5px\" style=\"background-image:revert!important;background-position:revert!important;background-size:revert!important;background-repeat:revert!important;background-origin:revert!important;background-clip:revert!important;border:revert!important;direction:revert!important;display:revert!important;height:revert!important;letter-spacing:revert!important;line-height:revert!important;margin:revert!important;opacity:revert!important;outline:revert!important;overflow:revert!important;table-layout:revert!important;text-indent:revert!important;text-orientation:revert!important;text-overflow:revert!important;text-transform:revert!important;vertical-align:revert!important;white-space:revert!important;word-break:revert!important;word-spacing:revert!important;writing-mode:revert!important;zoom:revert!important;width:75px!important;background-color:rgb(234,234,234)!important;padding:7px 5px!important;font-family:wf_segoe-ui_normal,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP&quot;,Tahoma,Arial,sans-serif!important;font-size:12px!important;font-weight:normal!important;color:rgb(33,33,33)!important;text-align:left!important\"></td></tr></tbody></table><div>Dear geomorph community,<br><br>I am working on a phylogenetic control requested by reviewers, and I would like to know whether extended.pgls() can be combined with trajectory.analysis().<br><br>My data and design<br>- Multivariate shape data (48 variables) for 195 individuals of 6 species, with many individuals per species.<br>- Species = species (factor); Stage = an ordered three-level factor (e.g., low, medium and high wear: S1, S2, S3). The goal is to build one trajectory per species, with the three stages as trajectory points, and to compare trajectories among species (length, direction, shape).<br>- Phylogeny: a pruned cladogram with branch lengths assigned (Grafen), with tips matching the levels of Species.<br><br>What I did<br><br>Ordinary model (works as expected):<br><br>fit_ordinary &lt;- procD.lm(Y ~ Species * Stage, data = my_data, iter = 999)<br>TA_ordinary &lt;- trajectory.analysis(fit_ordinary, groups = my_data$Species,<br>                                   traj.pts = my_data$Stage, pca = TRUE)<br><br>Here the trajectory points are exactly equal to the species-by-stage means of the individual scores in the PC space returned by plot(TA_ordinary).<br><br>Phylogenetic model:<br><br>fit_phylo &lt;- extended.pgls(Y ~ Species * Stage, data = my_data,<br>                           species = &quot;Species&quot;, phy = my_tree, iter = 999)<br>TA_phylo &lt;- trajectory.analysis(fit_phylo, groups = my_data$Species,<br>                                traj.pts = my_data$Stage, pca = TRUE)<br><br>trajectory.analysis() runs without errors, but the trajectory points do not match the data. For example, for one species (Species_A), comparing the mean of the individual scores in each stage with the trajectory point, both in the PC space of TA_phylo:<br><br>          mean of individuals       trajectory point<br>          PC1       PC2             PC1       PC2<br>S1       -0.257     0.060          -2.609     0.061<br>S2       -0.141     0.030          -1.802    -0.431<br>S3        0.249     0.134           2.423     0.585<br><br>My questions<br>1. Is trajectory.analysis() intended to work with objects of class <a href=\"http://lm.rrpp.ws\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://lm.rrpp.ws&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793953739942000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2ByK2AGaWcZXt_ZX3Sd10B\">lm.rrpp.ws</a> returned by extended.pgls()? If not, is there a recommended way to run a trajectory analysis conditioned on the phylogeny when each trajectory corresponds to a different species?<br>2. Is there any  limitation when the groups used for the trajectories (Species) are also the species used in the phylogenetic covariance structure?<br><br>Some cells are small (for example, n = 2 individuals in a few species-by-stage combinations), in case this is relevant.<br><br>I can provide a reproducible example or share the data  if that would help.<br><br>Thank you very much for your time.<br><br>Best regards,<br>Ale<br><br>geomorph_4.1.1<br>RRPP_2.2.0<p style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"></p>--<span> </span><br>You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;geomorph R package&quot; group.<br>To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to<span> </span><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-r-pack...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>To view this discussion, visit<span> </span><a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/geomorph-r-package/cbb6b0d7-9cd3-43bf-a6d0-ab4d56348312n%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/geomorph-r-package/cbb6b0d7-9cd3-43bf-a6d0-ab4d56348312n%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793953739942000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0UyPbOQUtPoKquDzPoqIKU\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/geomorph-r-package/cbb6b0d7-9cd3-43bf-a6d0-ab4d56348312n%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br></div></div><p style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-line:none;text-decoration-style:solid\"></p><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none;float:none;display:inline!important\">--<span> </span></span><br style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-line:none;text-decoration-style:solid\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none;float:none;display:inline!important\">You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;geomorph R package&quot; group.</span><br style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-line:none;text-decoration-style:solid\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none;float:none;display:inline!important\">To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to<span> </span></span><a href style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\" data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-r-pack...@googlegroups.com</a><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none;float:none;display:inline!important\">.</span><br style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-line:none;text-decoration-style:solid\"></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
